From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 store imports prompt when permissions grew (ABI 1.61)

Security audit RC-500 F-13, engine part. Bridge 0.64.0, feature
extension_install_sources. ReArcProfileInstallExtensionSources takes each Web
Store ID with the source browser's manifest.json. After the blocklist and
policy checks, ApprovedStoreInstaller compares the store manifest's required
permissions with the source manifest's using
PermissionMessageProvider::IsPrivilegeIncrease, the rule
ChromeExtensionRegistrarDelegate applies to updates. On an increase, or a
source manifest that does not parse, CreateInstallPrompt returns Chromium's
install prompt, which tab/050 routes to the host with its permission list.
ReArcProfileInstallExtensions keeps consent by ID.

Last rebased: 2026-11-10 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.96 (2ad9b7f5a8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

